{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1549128-vtr2e-homebrew-a-scale-each-day-keeps-the-dragons-at-bay","id":1549128,"title":"[VtR2E Homebrew] A Scale Each Day Keeps the Dragons At Bay","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-03-10T08:49:06-07:00","id":1549128,"title":"[VtR2E Homebrew] A Scale Each Day Keeps the Dragons At Bay","content":"Hello, all! I've been lurking around the homebrew and worldbuilding side of CofD for more than a little while now, so figured I'd finally take the opportunity to throw my hat into the ring and offer some of the things I've been working on. The idea behind this, specifically, is to challenge myself to write up a new Scale for each Coil of the Mysteries of the Dragon in current canon - so each Coil of the Ascendant, the Wyrm, the Voivode, Quintessence, Zirnitra, and Ziva will receive a Scale to go with it, plus a couple of extras if I feel any particularly concrete ideas. I cannot promise these will be balanced for play and you're welcome to suggest alterations and modifications, at the end of the night these are purely a fun thought exercise with some mechanical weight behind them, inspired by the lack of homebrew support for Coils compared to Theban Sorcery and Cruac.<br /> <br /> So, without further ado, I present the first in a long line of Scales of the Dragon!<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Subdermal Waking Aid</b></span><ul><li><b>Prerequisite Coil: </b><i>Surmounting the Daysleep</i></li> <li><b>Procedure: </b>The Dragon cuts into the subject's chest, bifurcating the sternum, and installs a labyrinthine network of electrodes, wires, and hermetically sealed mercury or lithium batteries around what remains of the myocardium, reminiscent of some abominable occult pacemaker. This surgical procedure requires an extended Intelligence + Medicine roll with a target of ten successes and an interval of one hour. If successful, this procedure can be reversed with an identical roll. This complex Scale is often used as practice by Dragons in preparation for developing greater and more complicated Scales further in their studies, inspired by the common idea among vampire hunters that Kindred are most vulnerable while slumbering in their havens and resting places. This Scale is intended to push the odds into a slumbering vampire's favour.</li> <li><b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The subject's heart is directly exposed to raw and unfiltered electrical pulses. Each time they awaken, the subject automatically descends into frenzy and suffers the Agonized (<i>GttN</i>, p.135) Persistent Condition for the entire night until the next time they settle down for daysleep.</li> <li><b>Failure:</b> Electrodes are wired incorrectly, significant valves and vessels necessary for the flow of Vitae are constricted by the device, the entire installation shifts out of place from the physical stress of awakening every night - something about the Scale is incompatible and refuses to take. The subject suffers from the Agonized (<i>GttN</i>, p.135) Condition for an hour each time they awaken from daysleep.</li> <li><b>Success:</b> The implant stimulates the subject's heart upon waking with a rhythmic pattern of refined electrical shocks, stabilizing the 'heart attack in reverse' suffered by most Kindred and energizing the flesh. For a number of turns equal to 3 + her Blood Potency after awakening from daysleep, including when it is interrupted by external factors, the subject gains a +5 dice bonus from spending Willpower on physical activity rolls instead of +3.</li> <li><b>Exceptional Success:</b> Once per week, instead of turns, the subject can decide to gain the benefits of the Scale after awakening from daysleep for one minute + an additional minute for each of the Dragon's dots in the Coil of the Ascendant.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23800-the-firebrand","name":"The Firebrand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23800_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-11T04:33:19-07:00","id":1549149,"title":"","content":"Good morning, all! Today's demonstrations focus on the Coil of the Ascendant, as admittedly that is the Mystery one of the players in my chronicle are exploring and experimenting with, so I wanted to write up some potential Scales of interest that she could discover and confront in the future. The first one - the <b>Regenerative Crimson Salve </b>- could be interpreted as a 'healing potion' so even though there're consequences for using it, I ultimately have mixed feelings about it even if I feel the natural Kindred inability to freely heal damage would be something that Dragons of the Ascendant Coil would be interested in surpassing. The Scale is ultimately limited by the fact it requires the subject to have the blush of life activated, thus ultimately only useful for Dragons with The Warm Face.<br /> <br /> The second Scale - <b>Hypersomnic Ritual</b> - is the opposite in that it's intended to preserve wounds through daysleep. I imagine for some Dragons it's not enough to simply decide when they sleep but also maintain a greater sense of agency over their unconscious body. It's not one of the great banes but daysleep as a natural vulnerability of Kindred, so in my mind it'd make sense to develop scales like the Hypersomnic Ritual and the Subdermal Waking Aid when you cannot stay awake at all hours of the day thus is really mostly useful for desperate neonates. Everybody has to start somewhere, I guess!<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Regenerative Crimson Salve</b></span><ul><li><b>Prerequisite Coil: </b><i>The Warm Face</i></li> <li><b>Procedure:</b> The Dragon prepares an infusion containing milk, honey, fresh blood, animal fat, and various arcane ingredients. Preparation to completion requires an extended Intelligence + Craft roll with a target of ten successes and an interval of 10 minutes. Failure means the Dragon can salvage their materials and try again, while a dramatic failure results in materials becoming unsalvageable and the Scale cannot be attempted again until the following night. Success allows the Dragon to create a single batch, enough for one subject, with an additional batch created per exceptional success.</li> <li><b>Outcome:</b> The end result is a blackish-crimson salve reeking of blood and corpse odour that remains potent for a number of hours equal to the Dragon's rating in the Coil of the Ascendant. The Dragon must spend 10 minutes applying the salve to their subject to gain its benefits, slathering it across their entire body and allowing it to soak through their flesh and into any open wounds. While the blush of life is active, the next time the subject spends Vitae to heal damage, the salve's effects activate and automatically heals one point of bashing damage 15 minutes afterwards as a mortal would - this effect repeats a number of times determined by the Dragon's rating in the Coil of the Ascendant, with \u2022 repeating once, \u2022\u2022 repeating twice, and \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 repeating a third time. If the subject is mortal, their healing is slightly accelerated to heal one point of bashing damage every 10 minutes a number of times equal to the Dragon's dots in the Coil of the Ascendant. The salve is horrifically pungent, imposing a -2 penalty to Social rolls with mortals as appropriate for an hour after application and allowing Kindred to treat their Blood Potency as one higher for the purposes of Kindred Senses when smelling the salve or its wearer.</li> </ul><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Hypersomnic Ritual</b></span><ul><li><b>Prerequisite Coil:</b> <i>Surmounting the Daysleep</i></li> <li><b>Procedure:</b> Before settling into daysleep, the Dragon covers their eyes, deafens their ears, and plugs their nose. They then undertake a ritual exercise resembling a mix of Tantric meditative techniques and a dance of grotesque and inhuman contortions, dislocating limbs and tearing ligaments, all the while falling in and out of near-torpid states of consciousness. This ritual exercise is an extended Stamina + Composure roll with a target of 10 successes and an interval of 10 minutes. The ritual exercise concludes with the expenditure of a single point of Willpower before the Dragon descends into slumber.</li> <li><b>Outcome:</b> The Dragon can automatically preserve up to three wounds during daysleep without expending Willpower, plus an additional wound for each exceptional success made during the extended roll. This Scale cannot be used to prevent healing changes such as tattoos, scars, piercings etc.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23800-the-firebrand","name":"The Firebrand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23800_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}